From 96f8fd24f6ed004d0d095a46788497d422d327ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bernhard=20Rosenkr=C3=A4nzer?= <bero@lindev.ch>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 03:30:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iconvdata: CP949 must not advance twice on a rejected KS C
 5601 pair (bug 35016)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GLIBC-SA-2026-0029 / CVE-2026-121757.  No Fix-Commit is on master.
CP949 is an alias of UHC.  The byte pair A2 E8 is a well-formed
KS C 5601 symbol (index 165) whose table entry is U+327E.  This
converter rejects that code point, but ksc5601_to_ucs4 has already
consumed the pair.  STANDARD_FROM_LOOP_ERR_HANDLER (2) then consumes
two more bytes.  With //IGNORE and the pair at the end of the buffer,
the decoder reads past the input.

Roll the pair back before the error handler.  //IGNORE then skips it
once, and the non-ignore path leaves the pointer on the illegal
sequence.  __UNKNOWN_10646_CHAR is only returned when the pair was
not consumed, so that path is unchanged.

Reported-by: Dickson Wu (SEAL & CertiK)
Signed-off-by: Bernhard Rosenkränzer <bero@lindev.ch>
---
